# The fusions whose composed figure is filed as the fusion's sum, per quantity. One row per (composed layer,
# quantity) where the composing document states no figure of its own and declares it the output of
# the fusion.
#
# Not owed, and not suspended either
#   The sum rule compares a filed figure with the sum of the parts. A figure filed as a `fusionSum`
#   derivation has declared itself that sum, so there is nothing to compare and the equality is not owed; nor has
#   anything gone missing, so nothing is suspended. composition/derived_quantities.sqlc computes the
#   figure, or names why it cannot, and composition/owed_equality.sqlc leaves these pairs out beside
#   the suspensions.
-- composition/fusion_quantities.sqlc filed as a derivation.
SELECT q.filing, q.layer, q.quantity
FROM (
    :compose(composition/fusion_quantities.sqlc)
) q
WHERE q.derivation IS NOT NULL
